<title>USA: Contract talks ongoing at Alcoa plant.</title>
<headline>Contract talks ongoing at Alcoa plant.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiations between Aluminum Co of America and the United Autoworkers union were continuing on Tuesday in an attempt to reach a new contract for workers at a forging plant in Cleveland, where the current pact expires on Tuesday at midnight EST, an Alcoa spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She declined to comment on any possibility of a strike or the nature of the talks.</p>
<p>&quot;All we've been told, is that they're still talking,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The current contract covers some 1,000 autoworkers at the plant, which makes forged aluminum parts for several industries, including the auto industry.</p>
<p>Union officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Pittsburgh newsroom -- 412-471-7088</p>
